  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "26 March 2015"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "The various parliamentary constituencies – all 650 of them – that combine to form the UK are often very different, diverse places. For instance, did you know:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "Kensington boasted both the highest average house price (£980,000) in England, Wales and Northern Ireland and the UK's highest average weekly wage (£848)?"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "89% of West Aberdeenshire and Kincardine residents stated that they were in good health, compared to 71% in the Rhondda?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
      "h3": null,
      "h4": null,
      "h5": null,
      "text": "Our interactive [cartogram](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartogram) visualises the constituencies as hexagons – making it simpler to see patterns in the data. Uncover and share your own stories."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "h2": null,
